  <static seed="354" source="Library/Michigan/Chap14Sec7/Q42.pg">
    <statement><p>Assume <m>z</m> is a smooth function of <m>x</m> and <m>y</m>.  If <m>z_{xy} = -4x</m>, what can you say about each of the following?</p>
<p><alert>(a)</alert>
<m>z_{yx}</m> = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert>(b)</alert>
<m>z_{xyx}</m> = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><alert>(c)</alert>
<m>z_{xyy}</m> = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4x</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>(a)</alert>
<m>z_{yx} = z_{xy} = -4x</m>.




<alert>(b)</alert>
<m>z_{xyx} = \frac{\partial}{\partial x}(z_{xy}) =
   \frac{\partial}{\partial x}(-4x) = -4</m>.




<alert>(c)</alert>
<m>z_{xyy} = \frac{\partial}{\partial y}(z_{xy}) =
   \frac{\partial}{\partial y}(-4x) = 0</m>.



</solution>
